<!--
    Mach-O bound pointer slots named for their import (`option machobinds
    on|off`, default on).

    kuna named an import slot only through the LC_DYSYMTAB indirect-symbol
    table, so a pointer slot that dyld fills through a bind record but that no
    indirect entry lists - a C function pointer or data pointer initialized to
    an import, an arm64e __auth_ptr, a vtable entry - read as an anonymous
    dat_<addr>. The bind records (chained-fixup binds and classic bind
    opcodes) name every such slot.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 environment-binding, the Mach-O bound-slot pass
    (`kuna-analysis/src/loader/kuna_machobinds.rs (MachoBindSlotsPass)`),
    committed at `read symbols`, so `option machobinds` is set after `load
    file`. The names go to the symbol table only, never the function inventory.

    The fixture `macho_bindslots_arm64` (built from
    `macho_bindslots_arm64.c`, local symbols stripped) has two __DATA,__data
    pointers bound by chained fixups to `_ext_handler` and `_ext_counter`;
    `dispatch` calls through the first and reads through the second. Both
    passes turn on `importdata`, which renders a data read through an import
    slot as the import.

    Pass 1 (machobinds off, the BUG): `(*dat_100004000)()` and
    `*dat_100004008`. Pass 2 (the default, the FIX): `ext_handler()` and `ext_counter`.
-->
